      "type": "solution",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "content": "$z = u^2v, u = \\sin t, v = e^t$，求 $\\frac{dz}{dt}$。",
      "answer": "$\\frac{dz}{dt} = e^t(\\sin^2t + 2\\sin t \\cos t) = e^t\\sin t(\\sin t + 2\\cos t)$",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "$\\frac{dz}{dt} = \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial u}\\frac{du}{dt} + \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial v}\\frac{dv}{dt}$",
        "$\\partial z/\\partial u = 2uv = 2\\sin t\\cdot e^t, \\frac{du}{dt} = \\cos t$",
        "$\\partial z/\\partial v = u^2 = \\sin^2t, \\frac{dv}{dt} = e^t$",
        "$\\frac{dz}{dt} = 2\\sin t\\cdot e^t\\cdot\\cos t + \\sin^2t\\cdot e^t = e^t(\\sin^2t + \\sin 2t)$"
      ],
